#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Package versions\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Versi pakej\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code on this page was developed using the following requirements.\n"
"We recommend using these versions or newer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod pada halaman ini dibangunkan menggunakan keperluan berikut.\n"
"Kami mengesyorkan menggunakan versi ini atau yang lebih baharu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"In quantum mechanics, observables correspond to physical properties that can be measured.\n"
"When considering a system of spins, for example, you could be interested in measuring the system's energy or obtaining information about the alignment of the spins, such as the magnetization or the correlations between spins.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Dalam mekanik kuantum, observable bersesuaian dengan sifat fizikal yang boleh diukur.\n"
"Apabila mempertimbangkan sistem spin, contohnya, anda mungkin berminat untuk mengukur tenaga sistem atau mendapatkan maklumat tentang penjajaran spin, seperti magnetisasi atau korelasi antara spin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To measure an $n$-qubit observable $O$ on a quantum computer, you must "
"represent it as a sum of tensor products of Pauli operators, that is\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mengukur observable $n$-Qubit $O$ pada komputer kuantum, anda mesti "
"mewakilinya sebagai jumlah hasil darab tensor operator Pauli, iaitu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"O = \\sum_{k=1}^K \\alpha_k P_k,~~ P_k \\in \\{I, X, Y, Z\\}^{\\otimes n},~~ \\alpha_k \\in \\mathbb{R},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"O = \\sum_{k=1}^K \\alpha_k P_k,~~ P_k \\in \\{I, X, Y, Z\\}^{\\otimes n},~~ \\alpha_k \\in \\mathbb{R},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "where\n"
msgstr "di mana\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"I = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"~~\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"~~\n"
"Y = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"~~\n"
"Z = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"I = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"~~\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"~~\n"
"Y = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & -i \\\\ i & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"~~\n"
"Z = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and you use the fact that an observable is Hermitian, as in, $O^\\dagger = "
"O$. If $O$ is not Hermitian it can still be decomposed as a sum of Paulis, "
"but the coefficient $\\alpha_k$ becomes complex.\n"
msgstr ""
"dan anda menggunakan fakta bahawa observable adalah Hermitian, iaitu "
"$O^\\dagger = O$. Jika $O$ bukan Hermitian, ia masih boleh didekomposisikan "
"sebagai jumlah Pauli, tetapi pekali $\\alpha_k$ menjadi kompleks.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In many cases, the observable is naturally specified in this representation after mapping the system of interest to qubits.\n"
"For example, a spin-1/2 system can be mapped to an Ising Hamiltonian\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam banyak kes, observable secara semula jadinya ditentukan dalam perwakilan ini selepas memetakan sistem yang diminati kepada qubit.\n"
"Contohnya, sistem spin-1/2 boleh dipetakan kepada Hamiltonian Ising\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\sum_{\\langle i, j\\rangle} Z_i Z_j - \\sum_{i=1}^n X_i,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\sum_{\\langle i, j\\rangle} Z_i Z_j - \\sum_{i=1}^n X_i,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the indices $\\langle i, j\\rangle$ run over interacting spins and the spins are subject to a transverse field in $X$.\n"
"The subscript index indicates which qubit the Pauli operator acts on, i.e. $X_i$ applies an $X$ operator on qubit $i$ and leaves the rest unchanged.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana indeks $\\langle i, j\\rangle$ berjalan ke atas spin yang berinteraksi dan spin tertakluk kepada medan melintang dalam $X$.\n"
"Indeks subskrip menunjukkan qubit mana yang operator Pauli bertindak ke atasnya, iaitu $X_i$ menggunakan operator $X$ pada qubit $i$ dan membiarkan yang lain tidak berubah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the Qiskit SDK, this Hamiltonian could be constructed with the following "
"code.\n"
msgstr "Dalam Qiskit SDK, Hamiltonian ini boleh dibina dengan kod berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we would like to measure the energy the observable is the Hamiltonian itself. Alternatively, we could be\n"
"interested in measuring system properties like the average magnetization by counting the number of spins\n"
"aligned in the $Z$-direction with the observable\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika kita ingin mengukur tenaga, observable-nya ialah Hamiltonian itu sendiri. Sebagai alternatif, kita mungkin\n"
"berminat untuk mengukur sifat sistem seperti purata magnetisasi dengan mengira bilangan spin\n"
"yang disejajarkan dalam arah $Z$ dengan observable\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"O = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1} Z_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"O = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1} Z_i\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For observables that are not given in terms of Pauli operators but in a matrix form, we first have to reformulate them\n"
"in the Pauli basis in order to evaluate them on a quantum computer.\n"
"We are always able to find such a representation as the Pauli matrices form a basis for the Hermitian $2^n \\times 2^n$ matrices.\n"
"We expand the observable $O$ as\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk observable yang tidak diberikan dalam bentuk operator Pauli tetapi dalam bentuk matriks, kita perlu terlebih dahulu memformulasikannya semula\n"
"dalam asas Pauli agar dapat menilainya pada komputer kuantum.\n"
"Kita sentiasa boleh menemui perwakilan sedemikian kerana matriks Pauli membentuk asas bagi matriks Hermitian $2^n \\times 2^n$.\n"
"Kita kembangkan observable $O$ sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"O = \\sum_{P \\in \\{I, X, Y, Z\\}^{\\otimes n}} \\mathrm{Tr}(O P) P,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"O = \\sum_{P \\in \\{I, X, Y, Z\\}^{\\otimes n}} \\mathrm{Tr}(O P) P,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the sum runs over all possible $n$-qubit Pauli terms and $\\mathrm{Tr}(\\cdot)$ is the trace of a matrix, which acts as inner product.\n"
"You can implement this decomposition  from a matrix to Pauli terms using the `SparsePauliOp.from_operator` method, like so:\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana jumlah berjalan ke atas semua sebutan Pauli $n$-Qubit yang mungkin dan $\\mathrm{Tr}(\\cdot)$ ialah jejak matriks, yang bertindak sebagai hasil darab dalam.\n"
"Anda boleh melaksanakan penguraian daripada matriks kepada sebutan Pauli ini menggunakan kaedah `SparsePauliOp.from_operator`, seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This means the matrix can be written as Pauli terms as $O = -Z_1 + 0.5 X_2 +"
" Y_2 Y_1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini bermakna matriks boleh ditulis sebagai sebutan Pauli sebagai $O = -Z_1 +"
" 0.5 X_2 + Y_2 Y_1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"  Remember the tensor product order maps to qubits as $q_n \\otimes q_{n-1} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes q_1$.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ingat bahawa susunan hasil darab tensor dipetakan kepada qubit sebagai $q_n \\otimes q_{n-1} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes q_1$.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"  If the observable is Hermitian (meaning $O^\\dagger = O$), the Pauli coefficients are real numbers.\n"
"  We can, however, also decompose any other complex matrix in terms of Paulis, if we allow for complex-valued coefficients.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"  Jika observable adalah Hermitian (bermakna $O^\\dagger = O$), pekali Pauli adalah nombor nyata.\n"
"  Namun, kita juga boleh menguraikan mana-mana matriks kompleks lain dalam bentuk Pauli, jika kita membenarkan pekali bernilai kompleks.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Measure in Pauli bases {#measure-in-pauli-bases}"
msgstr "Ukur dalam asas Pauli {#measure-in-pauli-bases}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A measurement projects the qubit state to the computational basis $\\{|0\\rangle, |1\\rangle\\}$. This implies that you can only measure observables that are diagonal in this basis, such as Paulis consisting only of $I$ and $Z$ terms.\n"
"Measuring arbitrary Pauli terms therefore requires a change of basis to diagonalize them. To do this, perform the following transformations,\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengukuran mengunjurkan keadaan qubit kepada asas pengiraan $\\{|0\\rangle, |1\\rangle\\}$. Ini bermakna anda hanya boleh mengukur observable yang pepenjuru dalam asas ini, seperti Pauli yang hanya terdiri daripada sebutan $I$ dan $Z$.\n"
"Oleh itu, mengukur sebutan Pauli sewenang-wenangnya memerlukan perubahan asas untuk menjadikannya pepenjuru. Untuk melakukan ini, lakukan transformasi berikut,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"    X &\\rightarrow Z = H X H \\\\\n"
"    Y &\\rightarrow Z = H S^\\dagger Y S H,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"    X &\\rightarrow Z = H X H \\\\\n"
"    Y &\\rightarrow Z = H S^\\dagger Y S H,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $H$ is the Hadamard gate and $S = \\sqrt{Z}$ is sometimes referred to as the phase gate.\n"
"If you are using an [Estimator](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.primitives.Estimator) to compute expectation values, the basis transformations are automatically performed.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $H$ ialah gate Hadamard dan $S = \\sqrt{Z}$ kadangkala dirujuk sebagai gate fasa.\n"
"Jika anda menggunakan [Estimator](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.primitives.Estimator) untuk mengira nilai jangkaan, transformasi asas dilakukan secara automatik.\n"

